## Bevy version

f61e44db2824c0cc4b4815748c4d3f051002ada7 (latest main right now)

## Operating system & version

Arch Linux, Kernel 5.11.2-zen1-1-zen

## What you did

```rust
use bevy::prelude::*;

struct Component;

fn main() {
    App::build()
        .add_plugins(DefaultPlugins)
        .add_startup_system(setup.system())
        .add_system(insert_component_system.system().label("send"))
        .add_stage_after(CoreStage::Update, "CustomStage", SystemStage::single(count_entities.system()))
        // this works fine, though: .add_system(count_entities.system().label("receive").after("send"))
        .run();
}

fn setup(mut commands: Commands) {
    commands.spawn(()).spawn(()).spawn(());
}

fn insert_component_system(
    keyboard: Res<Input<KeyCode>>,
    query: Query<Entity>,
    mut commands: Commands,
) {
    if keyboard.just_pressed(KeyCode::Return) {
        for entity in query.iter() {
            // without this line it seems to work fine
            commands.insert(entity, Component);

            break;
        }
    }
}

fn count_entities(query: Query<Entity>) {
    println!("entities: {}", query.iter().len());
}
```

## What you expected to happen

Even after pressing the return key, it should print out "entities: 3".

## What actually happened

After each press of the return key, the number decreased by one (eg. "entities: 2", ...)

## Additional information

Moving the counting system into the same stage as the modifying system seems to resolve the issue.

Since we're not iterating through all entities, could a possible cause be that the query iteration progress is shared between queries of different stages?

This is the minimal reproducing code I could construct. The original code worked fine on 0.4, but while trying to upgrade to `main` this came up.

An alternative repro is the following, without the `break`:
```rust
use bevy::prelude::*;

struct ComponentA;
struct ComponentB;

fn main() {
    App::build()
        .add_plugins(DefaultPlugins)
        .add_startup_system(setup.system())
        .add_system(insert_component_system.system().label("send"))
        .add_stage_after(CoreStage::Update, "CustomStage", SystemStage::single(count_entities.system()))
        // this works fine, though: .add_system(count_entities.system().label("receive").after("send"))
        .run();
}

fn setup(mut commands: Commands) {
    commands.spawn(()).with(ComponentA).spawn(()).spawn(());
}

fn insert_component_system(
    keyboard: Res<Input<KeyCode>>,
    query: Query<Entity, With<ComponentA>>,
    mut commands: Commands,
) {
    if keyboard.just_pressed(KeyCode::Return) {
        for entity in query.iter() {
            commands.insert(entity, ComponentB);
        }
    }
}

fn count_entities(query: Query<Entity>) {
    println!("entities: {}", query.iter().len());
}
```
